<title>SINGAPORE: Keppel FELS wins US$60 mln rig order.</title>
<headline>Keppel FELS wins US$60 mln rig order.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Keppel FELS said on Wednesday its U.S. subsidiary AMFELS Inc has won a US$60 million contract to build a jack-up drilling rig with Chiles Offshore Inc of Houston.  </p>
<p>The rig, the first newbuilding jack-up drilling order to be constructed by AMFELS, will be built under a license agreement with LeTourneau Inc, a subsidiary of the Rowan Companies Inc, a company statement said.</p>
<p>Work would start immediately and was expected to be completed in early 1999, it said.</p>
<p>It said Chiles Offshore planned to build a series of drilling units over the next several years.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
